If the current branch ref file doesn't exist (common when refs are packed and no loose ref is present yet), watchFile() returns undefined and no branch watcher is installed. In that state, new commits on the current branch typically won't touch .git/HEAD or packed-refs, so git state changes can be missed entirely. Consider adding a fallback watcher (e.g., watch the refs/heads directory or retry installing the branch watcher on 'rename'/packed-refs events) so commits are still detected when the ref file is created later.
```suggestion
      const branchRefPath = join(gitDir, branchRef);
      const watcher = this.watchFile('branch', branchRefPath, () => {
        this.emitGitStateChange();
      });

      // If the branch ref file does not exist yet (e.g., refs are packed),
      // fall back to watching the refs/heads directory so we can retry
      // installing the branch watcher when the ref file is created later.
      if (!watcher) {
        const headsDir = join(gitDir, 'refs', 'heads');
        this.watchFile('branch', headsDir, () => {
          if (this.gitStateCallbacks.size === 0) {
            return;
          }

          // The directory changed; attempt to reconfigure the branch watcher.
          void this.configureBranchWatcher(gitDir);
          this.emitGitStateChange();
        });
      }
```

When a watcher emits an `error`, the handler closes it and removes it from `this.watchers`, but there’s no attempt to re-establish watchers. If this happens (e.g. transient FS watcher errors), git state change detection will silently stop for the lifetime of the provider. Consider triggering a watcher re-setup (with backoff) when an error occurs while callbacks are registered.
```suggestion
    // Retry state is kept local to this watcher setup invocation.
    let remainingRetries = 5;
    let retryDelayMs = 1000;

    const createWatcher = (): FSWatcher | undefined => {
      if (!this.isWatcherSetupCurrent(generation)) {
        return undefined;
      }

      try {
        const watcher = this.fileSystem.watch(filePath, { persistent: false }, () => {
          if (this.isWatcherSetupCurrent(generation)) {
            onChange();
          }
        });

        if (!this.isWatcherSetupCurrent(generation)) {
          watcher.close();
          return undefined;
        }

        watcher.on('error', () => {
          watcher.close();
          if (this.watchers[key] === watcher) {
            delete this.watchers[key];
          }

          if (!this.isWatcherSetupCurrent(generation)) {
            return;
          }

          if (remainingRetries > 0) {
            const delay = retryDelayMs;
            remainingRetries -= 1;
            retryDelayMs *= 2;

            setTimeout(() => {
              if (!this.isWatcherSetupCurrent(generation)) {
                return;
              }
              createWatcher();
            }, delay);
          }
        });

        this.clearWatcher(key);
        this.watchers[key] = watcher;
        return watcher;
      } catch (error) {
        if (this.isEnoentError(error)) {
          return undefined;
        }

        throw error;
      }
    };

    return createWatcher();
```

_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_

**Stop retrying watcher setup forever when a generation installs nothing.**

If `setupWatchers()` finishes with `this.watchers` still empty—e.g. `git rev-parse` fails outside a repo, `.git` is missing, or every watched path returns `ENOENT`—this `while` loop immediately starts another setup cycle. Because the caller fire-and-forgets `ensureWatchers()`, that becomes an unbounded background loop of `git`/fs work instead of a graceful no-op.


<details>
<summary>💡 One way to gate retries to stale generations only</summary>

```diff
   private readonly gitStateCallbacks = new Set<GitStateChangeCallback>();
   private readonly watchers: Partial<Record<WatcherKey, FSWatcher>> = {};
   private watcherSetupInFlight: Promise<void> | undefined;
+  private watcherSetupInFlightGeneration: number | undefined;
   private watcherSetupGeneration = 0;
@@
   private async ensureWatchers(): Promise<void> {
     while (this.gitStateCallbacks.size > 0 && Object.keys(this.watchers).length === 0) {
       if (!this.watcherSetupInFlight) {
-        this.watcherSetupInFlight = this.setupWatchers(this.watcherSetupGeneration);
+        this.watcherSetupInFlightGeneration = this.watcherSetupGeneration;
+        this.watcherSetupInFlight = this.setupWatchers(this.watcherSetupInFlightGeneration);
       }

+      const awaitedGeneration = this.watcherSetupInFlightGeneration;
       await this.watcherSetupInFlight;
+
+      if (awaitedGeneration === this.watcherSetupGeneration) {
+        break;
+      }
     }
   }
@@
