`configureBranchWatcher` is started with `void ...` from an FS watch callback. If `configureBranchWatcher()` ever rejects (e.g. read errors other than ENOENT), this becomes an unhandled promise rejection and can crash or destabilize the process. Wrap the async call in a `.catch(...)` (or make the callback async and handle errors) and consider triggering `scheduleWatcherRebuild()` on failure.
```suggestion
        void this.configureBranchWatcher(gitDir, generation).catch(() => {
          // Prevent unhandled promise rejections from the watcher callback.
        });
```

